# Git ignore rules — git is the PUBLIC mirror of the Lore repo (decision 3 of the publication plan
# in the private `Plan-Private/` folder), and the delta between this file and `.loreignore` IS the
# privacy boundary:
#
#   * a path listed here but NOT in `.loreignore` is private — tracked by Lore, never reaching
#     the public git mirror (the "Private paths" block below is that list);
#   * everything else (build artifacts, runtime state, OS cruft) is noise that neither VCS
#     should hold, and MUST stay listed in both files — Lore reads only the root `.loreignore`,
#     so a rule added here or in any nested `.gitignore` is mirrored there by hand.
#
# `scripts/privacy-canary.mjs` scans the tracked-and-not-ignored set for private tokens, so a
# path that belongs in the private block but is missing from it surfaces there, not on GitHub.

# ── Private paths: Lore-tracked, git-ignored, never published ─────────────────────────────────
# Infrastructure and machine facts (server addresses, CI provisioning, agent notebooks), the
# machine-local Claude Code instructions, the private plans — which live in `Plan-Private/`,
# one folder rather than named files, so this file itself names no private plan — and the private
# reference game (Lore-only; the mirror keeps tracking it until the fresh root). Anchored at the
# root and listed as exact paths, so a same-named directory deeper in the tree is not swept along.
/.exarch/
/infra/
/ci/teamcity/
/CLAUDE.local.md
/Plan-Private/
/games/vigil/

# ── Noise: listed in BOTH ignore files ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Atomic-write temp files (`ludion_core::atomic::temp_sibling`, `scripts/atomic-write.mjs`): a kill
# mid-write leaves `.{name}.{pid}.{n}.tmp` in a content dir, and a path-scoped commit would stage it.
.*.[0-9]*.[0-9]*.tmp

# Rust build artifacts
/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# `ludion test`'s per-project scratch output (diff artifacts for failing golden tests: never
# committed, unlike the goldens themselves). Matches the workspace `target/` convention even for
# project directories with no Cargo.toml of their own (e.g. `examples/gallery/target/testkit`).
**/target/testkit

# npm toolchain, isolated to `editor/` (engine-architecture.md §6) — installed packages are never
# committed; `package-lock.json` is, so `npm ci` stays reproducible.
editor/**/node_modules/

# `scripts/check.mjs` per-step logs — throwaway, recreated every run. Unanchored, at any depth: the
# root one is the check script's, and a crate that runs its own verify (`crates/ludion-mcp/`) keeps a
# build cache under the same name. An anchored rule missed the nested one, and a path-less
# `commit.mjs` then swept 4961 build artifacts into the history.
.build/

# `ludion gen` run folders — candidate images and meshes downloaded from a ComfyUI server, one
# folder per run (`Plan/comfy-generation.md` decision 13). Recipes and workflows beside them are
# committed; the runs are scratch, noise in both VCSs. An accepted candidate is copied out by
# `gen accept` and committed from its destination.
/generation/runs/
**/generation/runs/


# Lore workspace state (source-control transition: Lore is the source of truth, git the
# derived mirror; both live in this directory). Git must never sweep Lore's local store.
/.lore/

# Hands-on testing guide for the human developer — declares itself a local, uncommitted note.
/TESTING.md

# Editor / OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# E5 player-profile saves - host-written runtime state (ludion::run only), never committed.
# The save dir sits under the game's PROJECT ROOT, which for games that root at their scene
# directory (vigil) is `scenes/` - hence the second pattern.
games/*/save/
games/*/scenes/save/
examples/*/save/

# Editor->agent context bridge (editor-views arc): host-written runtime state, never committed.
# `.ludion/` is the per-project editor scratch dir (the editor writes editor-context.json there).
.ludion/

# Claude Code machine-local state (.claude/skills/ IS tracked — never blanket-ignore .claude/).
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.json
/.claude/routines/.state/
/.claude/worktrees/
/.claude/checkpoints/
/.claude/mailbox/
/.claude/agent-registry.json
/.claude/agent-memory-local
/.claude/first-run
/.claude/assistant-daemon-state.json

# The private ComfyUI kit's rotating server logs (`infra/comfyui/run.ps1` writes one per launch);
# the smoke transcripts beside them are kept as records.
infra/comfyui/logs/comfyui*.log

# Python bytecode Blender writes beside the town kit scripts.
__pycache__/

# Derived by `ludion sync` from games/vigil/art/town; noise, so ignored in both VCSs.
/games/vigil/assets/town/

# Proptest persistence is off repo-wide (fixed seeds); a stray regression file is noise.
*.proptest-regressions
